- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MeasurementPlannerTests`

**How to implement.** The Planner's numerical layer reproduces the existing facts over their own designs (001 §M 'Full rank, `MuellerInverseTests`: "the full measurement set is well conditioned and every parameter is observable". The planner reports full rank for that design'; 'Layer 2 / Cramér–Rao, `MuellerInverseTests`: "an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers every constant, and its scatter IS what one fit's own covariance predicts". The planner's bounds for that design equal the promoted `predictedRelativeErrors`, and likewise for AT-2's design'; the S14.2 brief; 001 §W: no new inverse-physics test). The facts join `BerremanTests.MeasurementPlannerTests` (`Berreman/BerremanTests/MeasurementPlannerTests.fs`, step 475), which opens `PlannerInformation`, `MuellerFitting`, `FitUncertainty`, `RecoveryEnsembles` and `BenchNoise` where the compiler asks and names each design by its module, as step 475 does. AT-2's design is read at design level, as the S14.1 mapper recorded: AT-2's committed kit carries each cut on its observation rows (step 433). (1) `the planner finds the full C1-C4 set full rank with every quartz constant bounded, and C1 alone blind to n_e and g33`: over the four names of `UniaxialParameters.axes`, `PlannerInformation.over` of the one candidate `candidateRowsOver QuartzSample.forward (QuartzSample.quartzScalingAround QuartzSample.quartz) QuartzSample.quartz NoiseParam.decentLab QuartzSample.fullConfigurations |> expectOk` (step 479: the nominal point the truth, the noise the bench's) has rank 4, no confounded combination, `conditionOpt` `Some` of a finite number and `scaledSigmasOpt` `Some` of four finite positive entries, so `boundsOver` its scaling answers a bound on each constant; over `QuartzSample.c1` alone the rank is 2, and the names the texts of its two confounded directions carry are exactly n_e and g33 (`C1 is completely blind to g33, which is why a second crystal cut is required`: their Jacobian columns are identically zero, the ablation `MuellerInverseTests` measures). (2) `the planner's bounds for the noisy quartz design are what one noisy fit's own covariance predicts`: `first = QuartzSample.recoverQuartzFromNoisy NoiseParam.decentLab (List.head BiaxialSample.ensembleSeeds) |> expectOk` (step 480; the ensemble fact's first experiment), `quality = first.fit.report` and `predicted = predictedRelativeErrors QuartzSample.quartz first.fit quality` (step 342); the planner's information is `PlannerInformation.over` the axis names of the one candidate `{ jacobian = MuellerFitting.residualJacobianAt first.fit.residual first.fit.solution.solution; noise = quality.reducedChiSquared.noiseVariance }` (steps 336, 477): the design's Jacobian where the fit stopped, which `reportFrom` takes there through the same `FitQuality.residualJacobian`, and the fit's residual level as the noise. For each constant, its bound of `boundsOver first.fit.scaling` divided by the magnitude of its axis's value in `QuartzSample.quartz` equals its `predicted` entry within 1e-12 relative: the Cramér–Rao bound at that noise is the covariance account the fit itself gives (step 477), in the same relative units. (3) `the planner's bounds for AT-2's noisy design are what one noisy fit's own covariance predicts`: the same over `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.recoverAbsorbingFromNoisy NoiseParam.decentLab (List.head AbsorbingBiaxialSample.noisySeeds) |> expectOk` (AT-2's design, `fullConfigurations` = a1 @ a2 @ a3, its fifteen components) and `predictedRelativeErrors AbsorbingBiaxialSample.absorbing first.fit quality`. Each failure names the constant, the planner's bound and the prediction. The class's runtime grows by one transparent and one absorbing noisy fit (`MuellerInverseTests`' ensemble fact measures about 45 s per transparent fit, `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` about 190 s per absorbing one).

**Acceptance.** After the facts land, the Planner's layer 2 MUST find the full C1-C4 set full rank with a bound on every quartz constant and C1 alone rank 2 with n_e and g33 confounded, and its Cramér–Rao bounds at a noisy fit's own residual level MUST equal the promoted `predictedRelativeErrors` of that fit for the quartz design and for AT-2's design; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class `BerremanTests.MeasurementPlannerTests`, including `the planner finds the full C1-C4 set full rank with every quartz constant bounded, and C1 alone blind to n_e and g33`, `the planner's bounds for the noisy quartz design are what one noisy fit's own covariance predicts` and `the planner's bounds for AT-2's noisy design are what one noisy fit's own covariance predicts`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
